{"format":"bench-library","formatVersion":1,"id":"nrf24-radio","name":"Radio (nRF24L01)","version":"1.0.0","author":"Bench Workshop","owner":"codeopen0-cpu","description":"The nRF24L01+ 2.4 GHz radio module (SPI): two boards send each other small messages (up to 32 bytes) with acknowledgements and retries, as the real chip does. Both need the same channel, data rate and address. Includes RF24.h.","category":"Wireless","needsApp":"0.4.0","code":"// nRF24L01+: the chip's own registers and SPI commands (as RF24.h uses them). All radios of this\r\n// library run in one thread, so a sent packet reaches the others straight away: the one listening on\r\n// the same channel and data rate, with a matching address, takes it into its receive queue (3 deep)\r\n// and, with auto-ack, the sender hears TX_DS; else it retries and gives up with MAX_RT.\r\nconst radios = new Set();\r\nconst ADDR5 = new Set([0x0a, 0x0b, 0x10]);\r\n\r\nbench.device('nrf24', (part) => {\r\n  const r = {\r\n    regs: new Array(0x20).fill(0),\r\n    addr: { 0x0a: [0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7], 0x0b: [0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2], 0x10: [0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7] },\r\n    rx: [], tx: [], powered: false, ce: false, ceRose: false, pos: [0, 0, 0], sent: 0, got: 0, lost: 0, name: part.name,\r\n  };\r\n  const R = r.regs;\r\n  const reset = () => {\r\n    R.fill(0);\r\n    R[0x00] = 0x08; R[0x01] = 0x3f; R[0x02] = 0x03; R[0x03] = 0x03; R[0x04] = 0x03; R[0x05] = 0x02; R[0x06] = 0x0e; R[0x07] = 0x0e;\r\n    R[0x0c] = 0xc3; R[0x0d] = 0xc4; R[0x0e] = 0xc5; R[0x0f] = 0xc6;\r\n    r.addr = { 0x0a: [0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7], 0x0b: [0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2, 0xc2], 0x10: [0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7, 0xe7] };\r\n    r.rx = []; r.tx = [];\r\n  };\r\n  reset();\r\n  radios.add(r);\r\n  const status = () => {\r\n    const pipe = r.rx.length ? r.rx[0].pipe : 7;\r\n    return (R[0x07] & 0x70) | (pipe << 1) | (r.tx.length >= 3 ? 1 : 0);\r\n  };\r\n  const fifoStatus = () => (r.tx.length >= 3 ? 0x20 : 0) | (r.tx.length ? 0 : 0x10) | (r.rx.length >= 3 ? 0x02 : 0) | (r.rx.length ? 0 : 0x01);\r\n  const regRead = (a) => (a === 0x07 ? status() : a === 0x17 ? fifoStatus() : R[a]);\r\n  const rate = (x) => (x.regs[0x06] & 0x20 ? 250 : x.regs[0x06] & 0x08 ? 2000 : 1000);\r\n  const pipeAddr = (x, p) => (p === 0 ? x.addr[0x0a] : p === 1 ? x.addr[0x0b] : [x.regs[0x0a + p], ...x.addr[0x0b].slice(1)]);\r\n  const awBytes = (x) => (x.regs[0x03] & 3) + 2;\r\n  // one packet out of the TX queue, through the air\r\n  const transmit = () => {\r\n    const pkt = r.tx[0];\r\n    const aw = awBytes(r);\r\n    const to = r.addr[0x10].slice(0, aw).join();\r\n    let taken = null;\r\n    for (const o of radios) {\r\n      if (o === r || !o.powered || !(o.regs[0x00] & 0x02) || !(o.regs[0x00] & 0x01) || !o.ce) continue;\r\n      if (o.regs[0x05] !== R[0x05] || rate(o) !== rate(r) || awBytes(o) !== aw) continue;\r\n      if (Math.hypot(o.pos[0] - r.pos[0], o.pos[1] - r.pos[1], o.pos[2] - r.pos[2]) > 10000) continue; // (100 m)\r\n      for (let p = 0; p < 6; p++) {\r\n        if (!(o.regs[0x02] & (1 << p)) || pipeAddr(o, p).slice(0, aw).join() !== to) continue;\r\n        if (o.rx.length >= 3) { taken = 'full'; break; }\r\n        const dyn = (o.regs[0x1d] & 0x04) && (o.regs[0x1c] & (1 << p));\r\n        const w = dyn ? pkt.data.length : o.regs[0x11 + p] & 63;\r\n        const data = pkt.data.slice(0, w);\r\n        while (data.length < w) data.push(0);\r\n        o.rx.push({ pipe: p, data });\r\n        o.regs[0x07] |= 0x40; // RX_DR\r\n        o.got++;\r\n        taken = 'ok';\r\n        break;\r\n      }\r\n      if (taken) break;\r\n    }\r\n    const autoAck = R[0x01] & 0x01 && !pkt.noAck;\r\n    if (taken === 'ok' || !autoAck) {\r\n      r.tx.shift();\r\n      R[0x07] |= 0x20; // TX_DS\r\n      r.sent++;\r\n    } else {\r\n      R[0x07] |= 0x10; // MAX_RT: the packet stays in the queue (flush it, or try again)\r\n      R[0x08] = ((R[0x08] & 0xf0) + 0x10) & 0xf0 | (R[0x04] & 0x0f);\r\n      r.lost++;\r\n    }\r\n  };\r\n  return {\r\n    spi: {\r\n      transfer(bytes) {\r\n        if (!r.powered) return bytes.map(() => 0);\r\n        const c = bytes[0] ?? 0xff;\r\n        const out = [status()];\r\n        const rest = bytes.slice(1);\r\n        if (c < 0x20) { // R_REGISTER\r\n          const a = c & 0x1f;\r\n          const v = ADDR5.has(a) ? r.addr[a] : [regRead(a)];\r\n          rest.forEach((_, i) => out.push(v[i] ?? 0));\r\n        } else if (c < 0x40) { // W_REGISTER\r\n          const a = c & 0x1f;\r\n          if (ADDR5.has(a)) { r.addr[a] = [...rest.slice(0, 5), ...r.addr[a].slice(rest.length)].slice(0, 5); }\r\n          else if (a === 0x07) R[0x07] &= ~(rest[0] & 0x70); // writing 1 clears a flag\r\n          else if (rest.length) R[a] = rest[0] & 255;\r\n          rest.forEach(() => out.push(0));\r\n        } else if (c === 0x61) { // R_RX_PAYLOAD\r\n          const p = r.rx.shift();\r\n          rest.forEach((_, i) => out.push(p?.data[i] ?? 0));\r\n          if (!r.rx.length) R[0x07] &= ~0x40;\r\n        } else if (c === 0x60) { // R_RX_PL_WID\r\n          out.push(r.rx[0]?.data.length ?? 0);\r\n        } else if (c === 0xa0 || c === 0xb0) { // W_TX_PAYLOAD (no ack)\r\n          if (r.tx.length < 3) r.tx.push({ data: rest.slice(0, 32), noAck: c === 0xb0 });\r\n          rest.forEach(() => out.push(0));\r\n        } else if (c === 0xe1) r.tx = [];\r\n        else if (c === 0xe2) { r.rx = []; R[0x07] &= ~0x40; }\r\n        else if (c === 0xe3) { /* REUSE_TX_PL */ }\r\n        else rest.forEach(() => out.push(0)); // NOP, ACTIVATE...\r\n        while (out.length < bytes.length) out.push(0);\r\n        return out;\r\n      },\r\n    },\r\n    edges(list) {\r\n      for (const [pin, lv] of list) if (pin === 'CE') { if (lv && !r.ce) r.ceRose = true; r.ce = !!lv; }\r\n    },\r\n    step(io) {\r\n      const v = io.supply('VCC', 'GND');\r\n      const on = v >= 1.9;\r\n      if (on && !r.powered) reset();\r\n      r.powered = on;\r\n      r.ce = io.level('CE') === 1;\r\n      r.pos = part.motion().pos;\r\n      if (!on) { io.release('IRQ'); io.release('MISO'); io.draw(0); return; }\r\n      const ptx = (R[0x00] & 0x02) && !(R[0x00] & 0x01);\r\n      if (ptx && (r.ce || r.ceRose) && r.tx.length && !(R[0x07] & 0x10)) transmit();\r\n      r.ceRose = false;\r\n      const irq = R[0x07] & 0x70 & ~(R[0x00] & 0x70);\r\n      io.drive('IRQ', irq ? 0 : v, 1);\r\n      io.draw(!(R[0x00] & 0x02) ? 0.0000009 : (R[0x00] & 0x01) && r.ce ? 0.0135 : 0.0003);\r\n    },\r\n    status() {\r\n      if (!r.powered) return ['no power (3.3 V)'];\r\n      const mode = !(R[0x00] & 0x02) ? 'powered down' : R[0x00] & 0x01 ? (r.ce ? 'listening' : 'receive mode, CE low') : 'transmit mode';\r\n      return [`${mode}, channel ${R[0x05]}, ${rate(r) >= 1000 ? `${rate(r) / 1000} Mbps` : '250 kbps'}`, `${r.sent} sent, ${r.got} received, ${r.lost} unanswered`];\r\n    },\r\n    dispose() { radios.delete(r); },\r\n  };\r\n});\r\n","sketch":{"RF24.h":{"classes":["RF24"],"exports":["RF24_PA_MIN","RF24_PA_LOW","RF24_PA_HIGH","RF24_PA_MAX","RF24_1MBPS","RF24_2MBPS","RF24_250KBPS","RF24_CRC_DISABLED","RF24_CRC_8","RF24_CRC_16"],"code":"// RF24.h (TMRh20's library), the parts most sketches use:\n//   RF24 radio(CE_PIN, CSN_PIN);  radio.begin();  radio.setPALevel(RF24_PA_LOW);\n//   const byte address[6] = \"00001\";  radio.openWritingPipe(address);  radio.stopListening();\n//   radio.write(&value, sizeof(value))  (true: the other end got it)\n//   radio.openReadingPipe(1, address);  radio.startListening();  if (radio.available()) radio.read(&value, sizeof(value));\n// What's sent are the bytes of what you hand it: an int is 2 bytes, a long or float 4, a char array its\n// characters (as on an Arduino UNO).\nconst RF24_PA_MIN = 0, RF24_PA_LOW = 1, RF24_PA_HIGH = 2, RF24_PA_MAX = 3;\nconst RF24_1MBPS = 0, RF24_2MBPS = 1, RF24_250KBPS = 2;\nconst RF24_CRC_DISABLED = 0, RF24_CRC_8 = 1, RF24_CRC_16 = 2;\n\n/** the bytes of a value handed to write(): a number, a text, an array, a \"&x\" */\nconst _rfBytes = (x, len) => {\n  const out = [];\n  const num = (v, type, size) => {\n    const b = new DataView(new ArrayBuffer(8));\n    if (type === 'f' || (size === 4 && !Number.isInteger(Number(v)) && type !== 'i' && type !== 'u')) { b.setFloat32(0, Number(v), true); return [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => b.getUint8(i)); }\n    if (size === 1) return [Number(v) & 255];\n    if (size === 2) { b.setInt16(0, Number(v) | 0, true); return [b.getUint8(0), b.getUint8(1)]; }\n    b.setInt32(0, Number(v) | 0, true); return [0, 1, 2, 3].map((i) => b.getUint8(i));\n  };\n  let v = x, type = '';\n  if (isRef(x)) { v = x.value; type = x.type; }\n  if (typeof v === 'string') for (const ch of v) out.push(ch.charCodeAt(0) & 255);\n  else if (v && typeof v === 'object' && typeof v.length === 'number') {\n    const size = v.length ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(len / v.length)) : 1;\n    for (let i = 0; i < v.length; i++) out.push(...(typeof v[i] === 'string' ? [v[i].charCodeAt(0) & 255] : num(v[i], '', size)));\n  } else if (typeof v === 'boolean' || type === 'b') out.push(v ? 1 : 0);\n  else out.push(...num(v ?? 0, type, Math.min(4, len)));\n  while (out.length < len) out.push(0);\n  return out.slice(0, len);\n};\n/** put received bytes into what read() was handed */\nconst _rfInto = (x, bytes, len) => {\n  const dv = new DataView(new Uint8Array(bytes.concat(new Array(8).fill(0))).buffer);\n  if (isRef(x)) {\n    const t = x.type, cur = x.value;\n    if (t === 's' || typeof cur === 'string') { let s = ''; for (const b of bytes) { if (!b) break; s += String.fromCharCode(b); } x.value = s; return; }\n    if (t === 'b') { x.value = !!bytes[0]; return; }\n    if (t === 'f') { x.value = dv.getFloat32(0, true); return; }\n    if (len === 1) x.value = bytes[0];\n    else if (len === 2) x.value = t === 'u' ? dv.getUint16(0, true) : dv.getInt16(0, true);\n    else x.value = t === 'u' ? dv.getUint32(0, true) : dv.getInt32(0, true);\n    return;\n  }\n  if (x && typeof x === 'object' && typeof x.length === 'number') {\n    const size = x.length ? Math.max(1, Math.floor(len / x.length)) : 1;\n    for (let i = 0; i < x.length; i++) {\n      const o = i * size;\n      x[i] = size === 1 ? bytes[o] ?? 0 : size === 2 ? dv.getInt16(o, true) : dv.getInt32(o, true);\n    }\n  }\n};\n/** an address: \"00001\" / \"1Node\" (its characters, as written), or a number (0xF0F0F0F0E1) */\nconst _rfAddr = (a, w = 5) => {\n  if (typeof a === 'string') return Array.from(a.slice(0, w), (c) => c.charCodeAt(0) & 255);\n  if (a && typeof a === 'object' && typeof a.length === 'number') return Array.from(a).slice(0, w).map((c) => (typeof c === 'string' ? c.charCodeAt(0) : Number(c)) & 255);\n  let n = Number(a); const out = [];\n  for (let i = 0; i < w; i++) { out.push(n % 256); n = Math.floor(n / 256); }\n  return out;\n};\n\nclass RF24 {\n  constructor(ce, csn) { this.ce = ce; this.csn = csn; this.size = 32; this.dyn = false; this.pipe0 = null; this.listening = false; this.ok = false; }\n  _x(bytes) { digitalWrite(this.csn, LOW); const r = SPI.transfer(bytes.slice()); digitalWrite(this.csn, HIGH); return r; }\n  _w(reg, v) { return this._x([0x20 | reg, ...(Array.isArray(v) ? v : [v & 255])])[0]; }\n  _r(reg, n = 1) { const r = this._x([reg & 0x1f, ...new Array(n).fill(0xff)]); return n === 1 ? r[1] : r.slice(1); }\n  get_status() { return this._x([0xff])[0]; }\n  begin() {\n    pinMode(this.ce, OUTPUT); pinMode(this.csn, OUTPUT);\n    digitalWrite(this.ce, LOW); digitalWrite(this.csn, HIGH);\n    SPI.begin();\n    delay(5);\n    this._w(0x04, 0x5f); // SETUP_RETR: 1500 us, 15 tries\n    this.setDataRate(RF24_1MBPS);\n    this._w(0x1d, 0); this._w(0x1c, 0); this._w(0x01, 0x3f); this._w(0x02, 0x03);\n    this.setPayloadSize(32);\n    this._w(0x03, 0x03);\n    this.setChannel(76);\n    this._w(0x07, 0x70);\n    this._x([0xe2]); this._x([0xe1]);\n    this._w(0x00, 0x0c); // CRC 16\n    this.powerUp();\n    this._w(0x00, this._r(0x00) & ~0x01); // transmit mode\n    this.ok = this.isChipConnected();\n    return this.ok;\n  }\n  isChipConnected() { const aw = this._r(0x03); return aw >= 1 && aw <= 3; }\n  failureDetected = false;\n  powerUp() { const c = this._r(0x00); if (!(c & 0x02)) { this._w(0x00, c | 0x02); delay(5); } }\n  powerDown() { digitalWrite(this.ce, LOW); this._w(0x00, this._r(0x00) & ~0x02); }\n  setChannel(ch) { this._w(0x05, Math.max(0, Math.min(125, ch))); }\n  getChannel() { return this._r(0x05); }\n  setPALevel(level) { this._w(0x06, (this._r(0x06) & 0xf8) | ((level & 3) << 1)); }\n  getPALevel() { return (this._r(0x06) >> 1) & 3; }\n  setDataRate(rate) {\n    let v = this._r(0x06) & ~0x28;\n    if (rate === RF24_250KBPS) v |= 0x20; else if (rate === RF24_2MBPS) v |= 0x08;\n    this._w(0x06, v);\n    return true;\n  }\n  getDataRate() { const v = this._r(0x06); return v & 0x20 ? RF24_250KBPS : v & 0x08 ? RF24_2MBPS : RF24_1MBPS; }\n  setCRCLength(l) { let c = this._r(0x00) & ~0x0c; if (l === RF24_CRC_8) c |= 0x08; else if (l === RF24_CRC_16) c |= 0x0c; this._w(0x00, c); }\n  disableCRC() { this._w(0x00, this._r(0x00) & ~0x08); }\n  setPayloadSize(n) { this.size = Math.max(1, Math.min(32, n)); for (let p = 0; p < 6; p++) this._w(0x11 + p, this.size); }\n  getPayloadSize() { return this.size; }\n  setAddressWidth(w) { this._w(0x03, Math.max(1, Math.min(3, w - 2))); }\n  setRetries(delayX, count) { this._w(0x04, ((delayX & 15) << 4) | (count & 15)); }\n  setAutoAck(a, b) {\n    if (b === undefined) this._w(0x01, a ? 0x3f : 0);\n    else { let v = this._r(0x01); v = b ? v | (1 << a) : v & ~(1 << a); this._w(0x01, v); }\n  }\n  enableDynamicPayloads() { this._w(0x1d, this._r(0x1d) | 0x04); this._w(0x1c, 0x3f); this.dyn = true; }\n  disableDynamicPayloads() { this._w(0x1d, this._r(0x1d) & ~0x04); this._w(0x1c, 0); this.dyn = false; }\n  enableAckPayload() {}\n  getDynamicPayloadSize() { return this._x([0x60, 0xff])[1]; }\n  openWritingPipe(address) {\n    const a = _rfAddr(address);\n    this._w(0x0a, a); this._w(0x10, a); // (pipe 0 hears the acknowledgement)\n    this.pipe0 = a;\n  }\n  openReadingPipe(pipe, address) {\n    const a = _rfAddr(address);\n    if (pipe === 0) { this.pipe0 = a; this._w(0x0a, a); }\n    else if (pipe === 1) this._w(0x0b, a);\n    else this._w(0x0a + pipe, a[0]);\n    if (!this.dyn) this._w(0x11 + pipe, this.size);\n    this._w(0x02, this._r(0x02) | (1 << pipe));\n  }\n  closeReadingPipe(pipe) { this._w(0x02, this._r(0x02) & ~(1 << pipe)); }\n  startListening() {\n    this.powerUp();\n    this._w(0x00, this._r(0x00) | 0x01);\n    this._w(0x07, 0x70);\n    digitalWrite(this.ce, HIGH);\n    if (this.pipe0) this._w(0x0a, this.pipe0);\n    this.listening = true;\n  }\n  stopListening() {\n    digitalWrite(this.ce, LOW);\n    delayMicroseconds(100);\n    this._w(0x00, this._r(0x00) & ~0x01);\n    this._w(0x02, this._r(0x02) | 0x01);\n    this.listening = false;\n  }\n  /** a message waiting? (available(&pipe) also says which pipe it came on) */\n  available(pipe) {\n    const fifo = this._r(0x17);\n    if (fifo & 0x01) return false;\n    if (pipe !== undefined) setRef(pipe, (this.get_status() >> 1) & 7);\n    return true;\n  }\n  read(buf, len) {\n    const n = this.dyn ? this.getDynamicPayloadSize() : this.size;\n    const r = this._x([0x61, ...new Array(n).fill(0xff)]).slice(1);\n    this._w(0x07, 0x40);\n    _rfInto(buf, r.slice(0, len), len);\n  }\n  /** send it and wait for the acknowledgement: true = the other end got it */\n  write(buf, len, multicast = false) {\n    const data = _rfBytes(buf, Math.min(32, len));\n    const payload = this.dyn ? data : data.concat(new Array(Math.max(0, this.size - data.length)).fill(0)).slice(0, this.size);\n    this._w(0x07, 0x70);\n    this._x([multicast ? 0xb0 : 0xa0, ...payload]);\n    digitalWrite(this.ce, HIGH);\n    delayMicroseconds(15);\n    const until = millis() + 95;\n    let st = 0;\n    for (;;) {\n      st = this.get_status();\n      if (st & 0x30) break;\n      if (millis() > until) { this.failureDetected = true; break; }\n      delay(1);\n    }\n    digitalWrite(this.ce, LOW);\n    this._w(0x07, 0x70);\n    if (st & 0x10) { this._x([0xe1]); return false; }\n    return !!(st & 0x20);\n  }\n  writeFast(buf, len) { return this.write(buf, len); }\n  txStandBy() { return true; }\n  flush_tx() { this._x([0xe1]); }\n  flush_rx() { this._x([0xe2]); }\n  testCarrier() { return false; }\n  testRPD() { return false; }\n  printDetails() {\n    Serial.print('STATUS = 0x'); Serial.println(this.get_status(), HEX);\n    Serial.print('RF_CH = '); Serial.println(this.getChannel());\n    Serial.print('Data rate = '); Serial.println(['1 Mbps', '2 Mbps', '250 kbps'][this.getDataRate()]);\n    Serial.print('Payload size = '); Serial.println(this.size);\n  }\n  printPrettyDetails() { this.printDetails(); }\n}\n"},"nRF24L01.h":{"exports":[],"code":"// nRF24L01.h: the chip's register names (RF24.h has what sketches need).\n"}},"parts":[{"id":"nrf24l01","name":"Radio (nRF24L01+)","description":"VCC 3.3 V (not 5 V!), GND, CE and CSN to any two pins, SCK, MOSI, MISO to the board's SPI pins, IRQ (LOW when something happened) optional. Range here: about 100 m. #include <SPI.h>, <RF24.h>; RF24 radio(CE, CSN); radio.begin(); radio.openWritingPipe(address); radio.write(&data, sizeof(data)); or openReadingPipe(1, address); startListening(); if (radio.available()) radio.read(&data, sizeof(data));","swatch":"#1f2a24","mass":3,"shape":[{"box":[3,0.12,1.55],"at":[0,0.06,0],"color":"#1f2a24"},{"box":[0.45,0.12,0.45],"at":[-0.3,0.18,0],"color":"#141416"},{"box":[1.2,0.02,1.2],"at":[0.8,0.125,0],"color":"#c9a050","collide":false}],"pinRows":[{"ids":["GND","CE","SCK","MISO"],"at":[-1.3,0,-0.381],"dir":"x","kinds":{"GND":"gnd","CE":"in","SCK":"in","MISO":"out"}},{"ids":["VCC","CSN","MOSI","IRQ"],"at":[-1.3,0,-0.127],"dir":"x","kinds":{"VCC":"vin","CSN":"in","MOSI":"in","IRQ":"out"},"extra":{"VCC":{"label":"VCC (3.3 V, not 5 V)","vmin":1.9,"vmax":3.6},"CSN":{"label":"CSN (chip select)","pulled":"up"},"IRQ":{"label":"IRQ (LOW = something happened)"}}}],"spi":{"sck":"SCK","mosi":"MOSI","miso":"MISO","cs":"CSN"},"device":"nrf24"}],"examples":[{"name":"Radio remote servo","description":"Two boards, two radios. Turn the knob on the left board's bench: it sends the angle 20 times a second; the right board steers its servo to it. Pull a radio's VCC wire off (or drag the boards 2 m apart) and the sender's serial monitor reports lost messages.","project":{"format":"bench-workshop","version":1,"name":"Radio remote servo","parts":[{"uid":"tx","type":"maker-board","name":"Sender","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[-16,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"radio1","type":"nrf24-radio/nrf24l01","name":"Radio 1","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-16,0,-9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"knob","type":"knob","name":"Knob","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[-16,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"rx","type":"maker-board","name":"Receiver","params":{"usb":true},"parent":null,"pos":[16,0,0],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"radio2","type":"nrf24-radio/nrf24l01","name":"Radio 2","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[16,0,-9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]},{"uid":"servo","type":"servo-sg90","name":"Servo","params":{},"parent":null,"pos":[16,0,9],"rot":[0,0,0,1]}],"wires":[{"id":"w1","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w2","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w3","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"CE"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w4","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GP17"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"CSN"},"color":"#9b59b6"},{"id":"w5","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GP18"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"SCK"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w6","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GP19"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"MOSI"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w7","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GP16"},"b":{"uid":"radio1","pin":"MISO"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w8","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"VCC"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w9","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GND"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w10","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP14"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"CE"},"color":"#f08a24"},{"id":"w11","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP17"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"CSN"},"color":"#9b59b6"},{"id":"w12","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP18"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"SCK"},"color":"#4a90e2"},{"id":"w13","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP19"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"MOSI"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w14","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP16"},"b":{"uid":"radio2","pin":"MISO"},"color":"#e8c547"},{"id":"w15","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"L"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w16","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"3V3"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"H"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w17","a":{"uid":"tx","pin":"A0"},"b":{"uid":"knob","pin":"W"},"color":"#3cb371"},{"id":"w18","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"5V"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"V+"},"color":"#e04848"},{"id":"w19","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GND2"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"GND"},"color":"#2b2d33"},{"id":"w20","a":{"uid":"rx","pin":"GP15"},"b":{"uid":"servo","pin":"SIG"},"color":"#e8c547"}],"programs":{"tx":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Radio remote, the sending end: turn the knob (its slider in the run panel); the angle goes out by\n// radio 20 times a second. radio.write() says whether the other end got it.\n#include <SPI.h>\n#include <RF24.h>\n\nRF24 radio(14, 17);            // CE, CSN\nconst byte address[6] = \"00001\";\nint sent = 0, lost = 0;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!radio.begin()) {\n    Serial.println(\"The radio isn't answering: check its wires (and 3.3 V)\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n  radio.openWritingPipe(address);\n  radio.setPALevel(RF24_PA_LOW);\n  radio.stopListening();\n}\n\nvoid loop() {\n  int angle = map(analogRead(A0), 0, 4095, 0, 180);\n  bool ok = radio.write(&angle, sizeof(angle));\n  if (ok) sent++; else lost++;\n  if ((sent + lost) % 20 == 0) {\n    Serial.print(\"angle \");\n    Serial.print(angle);\n    Serial.print(\"   got there: \");\n    Serial.print(sent);\n    Serial.print(\"   lost: \");\n    Serial.println(lost);\n  }\n  delay(50);\n}\n"},"rx":{"lang":"arduino","source":"// Radio remote, the receiving end: each angle that arrives turns the servo.\n#include <SPI.h>\n#include <RF24.h>\n#include <Servo.h>\n\nRF24 radio(14, 17);            // CE, CSN\nconst byte address[6] = \"00001\";\nServo servo;\n\nvoid setup() {\n  Serial.begin(115200);\n  if (!radio.begin()) {\n    Serial.println(\"The radio isn't answering: check its wires (and 3.3 V)\");\n    while (true) delay(100);\n  }\n  radio.openReadingPipe(0, address);\n  radio.setPALevel(RF24_PA_LOW);\n  radio.startListening();\n  servo.attach(15);\n}\n\nint last = -1;\n\nvoid loop() {\n  if (radio.available()) {\n    int angle = 0;\n    radio.read(&angle, sizeof(angle));\n    servo.write(angle);\n    if (angle != last) {\n      Serial.print(\"angle: \");\n      Serial.println(angle);\n      last = angle;\n    }\n  }\n}\n"}},"boards":[]}}]}